Inclusion Criteria:

1. Voluntarily signed the informed consent form (ICF);
2. Aged between 18-75 years old (inclusive);
3. Confirmed clinical diagnosis of primary light chain (AL) amyloidosis;
4. Relapsed or refractory disease;
5. dFLC ≥ 40 mg/L (based on central laboratory test results);
6. ECOG performance status of 0 to 2;
7. No active systemic infection within 2 weeks prior to leukapheresis;
8. Adequate bone marrow and major organ function (including hepatic, renal, cardiac, and pulmonary);

Exclusion Criteria:

1. Presence of any clinically significant cardiovascular disease within 6 months prior to screening;
2. Clinically significant central nervous system (CNS) disease or pathological abnormality;
3. History of solid organ transplantation (e.g., heart, lung, kidney, liver);
4. Presence of complete intestinal obstruction;
5. Moderate to severe pleural effusion or ascites that is difficult to control with conventional treatment and requires continuous catheter drainage;
6. History of malignancy within 5 years prior to signing the ICF
